{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SkewBranchingTwoOne","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SkewBranchingTwoOne","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SkewBranchingSum","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTHookFormula"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.rskIdentitiesContextInstance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.rskIdentitiesContextInstance","kind":"instance","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewBranchingTwoOne.lean#L75-L78","doc":"**The class is inhabited.**  `branching_two_one` and `c8_superexp` are now applicable at every\nconcrete `k ≥ 3`; until this instance existed neither was. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.branching_two_one_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.branching_two_one_holds","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewBranchingTwoOne.lean#L62-L73","doc":"**The classical branching identity at `μ = (2,1)`, unconditionally.**\n\n3 · ∑_{λ ⊢ k}  f^λ · f^{λ/(2,1)}  =  k!        (k ≥ 3)\n\nThis is what `RSKIdentitiesContext.branching_two_one` asks for, and it discharges the class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.sum_dimSYT_mul_fDimSkew_eq_skewPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.sum_dimSYT_mul_fDimSkew_eq_skewPair","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewBranchingTwoOne.lean#L52-L60","doc":"The `Nat.Partition`-indexed branching sum is `skewPair mu21`, reindexed by\n`partitionShapeEquiv`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.numStandardYoungTableaux_mu21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.numStandardYoungTableaux_mu21","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SkewBranchingTwoOne.lean#L47-L50","doc":"**`f^{(2,1)} = 2`** — the hook shape carries exactly two standard tableaux.  Read off the\n`decide`-verified small-`n` hook bridge; a computation on one shape, not the general HLF. ","signatureChunk":0}]}